Or we could kinda use the table from DD3(.5), which are more or less the 
same thing. Plus an effect concerning the number of attacks per round 
you get. When you to-hit bonus (Base Attack Bonus, BAB) reachs 6, you 
get a second attack, a third at 11 and a fourth at 16. fighter classes 
have max BAB 20 (1/XL) so 4 attacks (at +20/+15/+10/+5), spellcasters 
have max BAB 10 (.5/XL) so 2 attacks at +10/+5 making them much worst in 
melee. Monks have special bonuses for unarmed attacks (iirc with a max 
of 5 attacks/round instead of 3 at max level in DD3.5)

Globally, I like the combat system of DD3 and think that might be a good 
idea to try and implement it in nethack (maybe with some modifications 
such as different bonuses for melee/ranged). One of the trouble with 
that is that the DD3 system is highly intricated with the feat system 
and swapping from nethack skill system to DD3 feat system ask for 	a 
major rewrite of nethack...

Speaking of DD3, there is also the possibility to add special properties 
to items (weapon, armor, mundane rings or amulet,...) which could be a 
source of insipration for doing this kind of stuff in nethack (which 
I'll thing would be a nice idea but require a lot of work).

Off course, an upgraded item might count as an artefact and thus reduce 
chances of getting another one or even to manage upgrading another item...


